{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > obligation_read.py <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));m=json.load(open(r['audit_spec_path']))\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id']=='B-config-export':\n  b['unknowns']=[];b['external_effects']=['getStatus returns the cloned Config, with omitted AutoLeave defaulting false; it does not mutate the live configuration.']\n if b['id']=='B-read':\n  b['implementation_guards']+=['Singleton shortcut checks only one incoming voter and no outgoing voters; it does not check the responder is that voter before producing a ReadState.','ReadIndex requests may be lost and the caller must retry with appropriate request context; missing response alone is not a progress violation.']\n  b['source_ids']=list(dict.fromkeys(b['source_ids']+['s-singleton','s-read-safe-contract','s-read-caller-contract']))\n  b['unknowns']=['Whether local-only singleton ReadState production remains eligible after the responder is removed while StepDownOnRemoval is false.','Detailed repeated RequestCtx and membership-transition histories remain outside this question.']\nm['core_overview']['open_details']=[x for x in m['core_overview']['open_details'] if 'Configuration-copy/status' not in x]\nm['core_overview']['open_details'].append('Singleton read-response eligibility after self-removal with optional step-down disabled.')\n# Related handoff records only source meaning; fixed execution identities stay in feedback.\njson.dump(m,open('map-read.json','w'),indent=2)\nq={'question':'Can a removed leader use the ReadOnlySafe singleton shortcut to emit ReadState without any post-request quorum communication when the sole installed voter is a different node?','importance':'A read barrier issued without eligible quorum authority can undermine the library read-safety mechanism. The examined component is response eligibility, not a completed stale application read.','source_ids':[