ton support can authorize a returned ReadState only when the responder itself is the sole voter in its installed configuration. A removed node cannot count itself as the different sole voter.','source_ids':['s-read-safe-contract','s-singleton','s-auto-contract','s-read-caller-contract','src-quorum','s-majority'],'scope':{'description':'Necessary local-support eligibility for ReadOnlySafe singleton responses after applied self-removal, with optional immediate step-down disabled and zero post-request peer communication.','assumptions':['Non-Byzantine peers, unique new read context, serialized RawNode methods and valid applied membership history.','No quorum acknowledgment or other network message reaches the responder after the request.'],'excluded':['No client read completion or stale returned application value is claimed; the documented application-wait condition remains outside the endpoint.','No liveness obligation to answer a read; no response is permitted.','No claim about lease reads, general dynamic quorum histories or arbitrary reuse of contexts.']},'pending':[],'grounding':{'source_ids':['s-leader','s-singleton','src-config','s-removal-option','s-read-send'],'expectation_ids':['s-read-safe-contract','src-quorum','s-majority'],'binding_ids':['bind-singleton-test','bind-singleton-read'],'derivation':'ReadOnlySafe obtains read authority by communicating with a quorum. The local singleton exception is valid because the local voter is then a quorum itself, as IsSingleton documentation assumes. MajorityConfig counts only IDs in its voter set. When the local responder is absent and no communication occurs, it has no eligible voter support for the fresh request; role state alone cannot supply it. Optional step-down changes behavior but does not weaken the separately selected ReadOnlySafe guarantee. This is a necessary support condition, not a guarantee of read completion or an equality requiring success.','applicability':'Fresh request after actual applied removal, singleton voter other than responder, no network input to responder through returned Ready.','unresolved':[],'alternatives':['Enabling step-down protects this history; dropping or forwarding the request without producing unsupported ReadState is permitted.','Application wait may prevent an immediate client read, but does not provide missing quorum support for this library-issued barrier.'],'conflicts':[]}}\nb=[]\nfor i,mat,sym,a,z,desc in [('bind-singleton-test','s-singleton','IsSingleton',160,162,'Cardinality-only singleton test.'),('bind-singleton-read','s-leader','stepLeader',1340,1365,'ReadIndex shortcut emits local commit before current-term and quorum paths.')]:b.append(dict(id=i,material_id=mat,symbol=sym,start_line=a,end_line=z,description=desc,pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id='O-read-singleton',source_ids=[mat],rationale=desc)]))\nchanges={i:{'impact':'clarification','source_ids':['s-singleton','s-read-safe-contract','s-read-caller-contract','s-config-clone','s-status-copy'],'rationale':'Clarify known singleton guard and request-loss contract, and replace answered copy uncertainty with source relationship.','preserves':'Earlier automatic-exit and status-copy requirements and witnesses are unchanged; the new question addresses independent read support eligibility.'} for i in ['B-read','B-config-export','core_overview']}\ns={'action':'obligation','rationale':'Fix a narrow independently sourced read-support eligibility responsibility, retaining the unobserved client endpoint and optional-step-down counterevidence.','question':q,'obligation':claim,'bindings':b,'map_path':'map-read.json','map_changes':changes,'feedback':{'ref_ids':['B-read','B-config','daa885484a134fa99fd3460aa3e93e7b','944f18350c7c45a2b9c3446138444540'],'answered':'Exploration executes self-removal leaving node 1 in StateLeader with voters [2], node 2 commits/applies new value at index 7, and node 1 produces a local ReadState at index 5 without communication. Step-down-enabled control produces none. This establishes reachability for an eligibility check, not a completed stale read. Status-copy correspondence is accepted and its map reminder is removed.','remaining':['Fresh fixed comparison of returned ReadState against necessary eligible local singleton support.','No client endpoint is established under the documented application-wait wording.'],'understanding':'updated','rationale':'Preserve precise scope and contrary evidence; do not turn permitted nonresponse into a failure.'}}\njson.dump(s,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2);print(subprocess.run(r['validation']['command']+['submission.json'],capture_output=True,text=True).stdout)\nPY\npython3 obligation_read.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
